WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.490 --> 00:00:04.580
Cymbal runs 40 pipelines from cron, on one small machine.

2
00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:06.990
When one fails, nobody knows.

3
00:00:07.010 --> 00:00:11.540
Turn them into DAGs that repeat, backfill, and shout when they break.

4
00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:14.550
A DAG is a recipe with steps in order.

5
00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:16.938
In Cloud Composer, you write it in Python.

6
00:00:16.958 --> 00:00:19.310
Tasks, and arrows between them.

7
00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:21.397
Composer only gives the orders.

8
00:00:21.417 --> 00:00:24.660
BigQuery and Dataflow do the cooking.

9
00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:28.320
The golden rule: a task must be safe to run twice.

10
00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:29.720
Tasks get retried.

11
00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:32.905
If each retry appends rows, you get duplicates.

12
00:00:32.925 --> 00:00:36.018
So overwrite the partition for that day, or use MERGE.

13
00:00:36.038 --> 00:00:38.765
Run it ten times: same result.

14
00:00:38.785 --> 00:00:41.690
The word for this is idempotent.

15
00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:44.150
Rule two: never ask the clock.

16
00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:47.285
Use the run date that Airflow gives you, not now.

17
00:00:47.305 --> 00:00:50.670
Then a backfill for last March really loads last March.

18
00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:55.920
Finally, add retries with a delay, a timeout, and an alert on failure.

19
00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:57.180
Recap.

20
00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:02.790
A good task is idempotent, uses the run date, retries, and is loud when it fails.

21
00:01:02.810 --> 00:01:05.585
Try the checkpoint below.
